  "detail": "How many rotated (about the origin) copies of the \"pyjama set\" $\\{(x, y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : \\operatorname{dist}(x, \\mathbb{Z}) \\leq \\varepsilon\\}$ are needed to cover $\\mathbb{R}^2$? The pyjama set is a union of vertical strips. This beautiful geometric problem, solved by Manners (2015), asks how many rotations are needed to cover the plane. It connects geometry, combinatorics, and Fourier analysis.",
