  "summary": "If a locally compact group acts faithfully and continuously on a manifold, must it be a Lie group?",
  "detail": "If a locally compact group acts faithfully and continuously on a manifold, must it be a Lie group? The Hilbert-Smith conjecture asks whether every locally compact group with a continuous faithful action on a manifold is necessarily a Lie group. This would rule out p-adic groups acting on manifolds, resolving a fundamental question about the symmetries of topological spaces.",
