  "summary": "Is $K \\times [0,1]$ collapsible for every finite contractible 2-dimensional CW complex K?",
  "detail": "Is $K \\times [0,1]$ collapsible for every finite contractible 2-dimensional CW complex K? The Zeeman conjecture predicts that the product of any finite contractible 2-complex with an interval is collapsible (can be reduced to a point by elementary collapses). This relates to the Poincaré conjecture and questions about higher-dimensional manifolds. A counterexample would have major implications.",
