  "summary": "For which nonzero $r \\in \\mathbb{Q}$ is it true that for every nontrivial knot $K \\subset S^{3}$ there is a homomorphism $$ \\pi_{1}(S^{3}_{r}(K)) \\to \\operatorname{SU}(2) $$ with n",
  "detail": "For which nonzero $r \\in \\mathbb{Q}$ is it true that for every nontrivial knot $K \\subset S^{3}$ there is a homomorphism $$ \\pi_{1}(S^{3}_{r}(K)) \\to \\operatorname{SU}(2) $$ with nonabelian image? Source: Kirby's Problems in Low-Dimensional Topology notes. Original problem number: KP-1.14. Literature notes: (1) If this statement is true for some $r \\in \\mathbb{Q}$, then it’s true for $-r$; hence, we assume $r > 0$. Kronheimer–Mrowka proved [KM04] that there is a homomorphism with nonabelian image for all $r \\in (0, 2]$. Work of Baldwin– Sivek [BS23a] together with announced results of Baldwin–Li–Sivek–Ye [BLSY24], and Farber–Reinoso–Wang [FRW24] proves the same for all $r \\in (2, 5)$ with prime power numerators. (2) Let $r = p/q > 0$ with $p$ and $q$ relatively prime, and assume that $\\Delta_{K}(\\zeta^{2}) \\neq$ 0 for any $p$th root of unity $\\zeta$. Then it is further known [BS23a] that if $\\pi_{1}(S^{3}_{r}(K))$ only admits abelian $\\operatorname{SU}(2)$-representations, then $K$ is fibered, strongly quasipositive, and $r \\geq 2g(K) - 1.$ (3) Note that for most $r \\in \\mathbb{Z}$, there is a torus knot whose $r$–surgery is $\\operatorname{SU}(2)$- abelian. Problem 3.51 deals with a related problem about the characteri- zation of rational homology spheres whose fundamental groups have only Abelian $\\operatorname{SU}(2)$ representations. References cited: - [KM04] P. B. Kronheimer and T. S. Mrowka. Dehn surgery, the fundamental group and $\\mathrm{SU}(2)$. Math. Res. Lett., 11(5-6):741–754, 2004. doi:10.4310/MRL.2004.v11.n6.a3. - [BS23a] John A. Baldwin and Steven Sivek. Instantons and L-space surgeries. J. Eur. Math. Soc. (JEMS), 25(10):4033–4122, 2023. doi:10.4171/jems/1280. - [BLSY24] John A. Baldwin, Zhenkun Li, Steven Sivek, and Fan Ye. Small Dehn surgery and $\\mathrm{SU}(2)$. Geom. Topol., 28(4):1891–1922, 2024. doi:10.2140/gt.2024.28.1891. - [FRW24] Ethan Farber, Braeden Reinoso, and Luya Wang. Fixed-point-free pseudo-Anosov homeomorphisms, knot Floer homology and the cinquefoil, 2024. doi:10.2140/gt.2024.28.4337.",
