  "summary": "(a) Compute the Khovanov homology for all torus knots $T(m, n)$. (b) Compute the Khovanov–Rozansky $\\mathfrak{g}\\mathfrak{l}(N)$ homology for all torus knots.",
  "detail": "(a) Compute the Khovanov homology for all torus knots $T(m, n)$. (b) Compute the Khovanov–Rozansky $\\mathfrak{g}\\mathfrak{l}(N)$ homology for all torus knots. Source: Kirby's Problems in Low-Dimensional Topology notes. Original problem number: KP-1.31. Literature notes: (1) The data for the Khovanov homology of $T(m, n)$ is available at [LM23b] for small $m, n$. Khovanov–Rozansky homology data is available at [Lew23a, Lew23b]. (2) The homology is known to have a lot of torsion [MPS $^{+}18$]. Comput- ing Khovanov homology with $\\mathbb{Z}_{2}$ coefficients and $\\mathfrak{g}\\mathfrak{l}(N)$ homology with $\\mathbb{Z}_{N}$ coefficients might be easier than rational coefficients [GOR13]. On the other hand, an open conjecture [PS14, MPS $^{+}18$] states that the Khovanov homology of $T(m, n)$ for $m$ prime and $n > m$ has $m$-torsion. (3) The triply graded Khovanov–Rozansky homology of torus knots (with in- teger coefficients) is computed in [Mel22]. By [Ras15] there is a spectral sequence from triply graded homology to Khovanov (resp. Khovanov– Rozansky) homology, but the differentials are not known explicitly. (4) By [Sto09], there is a well-defined limit of the Khovanov homology of $T(m, n)$ as $m \\to \\infty$, also known as $T(n, \\infty)$. Rozansky [Roz14] shows that the Khovanov homology of $T(n, \\infty)$ provides a categorified equivalent of the Jones–Wenzl projector [Wen87]. The triply graded homology of $T(n, \\infty)$ is computed in [Hog18], and precise conjectures for the Khovanov homology of $T(n, \\infty)$ are discussed in [GOR13, GL15]. (5) In contrast, the Heegaard Floer homology of $T(m, n)$ is well known [OS05b]. References cited: - [LM23b] Charles Livingston and Allison H. Moore. Knotinfo: Table of knot invariants, November 2023. https://knotinfo.org. - [Lew23a] Lukas Lewark. Foamho, an $\\mathfrak{sl}(3)$-homology calculator. URL: https://people.math.ethz.ch/ llewark/foamho.php, November 2023. - [Lew23b] Lukas Lewark. Khoca, a knot homology calculator. URL: https://people.math.ethz.ch/ llewark/khoca.php, November 2023. - [MPS+18] Sujoy Mukherjee, Józef H. Przytycki, Marithania Silvero, Xiao Wang, and Seung Yeop Yang. Search for torsion in Khovanov homology. Exp. Math., 27(4):488– 497, 2018. doi:10.1080/10586458.2017.1320242. - [GOR13] Eugene Gorsky, Alexei Oblomkov, and Jacob Rasmussen. On stable Khovanov homology of torus knots. Exp. Math., 22(3):265–281, 2013. doi:10.1080/10586458.2013.798553. - [PS14] Józef H. Przytycki and Radmila Sazdanović. Torsion in Khovanov homology of semi-adequate links. Fund. Math., 225(1):277–304, 2014. doi:10.4064/fm225-1-13. - [Mel22] Anton Mellit. Homology of torus knots. Geom. Topol., 26(1):47–70, 2022. doi: 10.2140/gt.2022.26.47. - [Ras15] Jacob Rasmussen. Some differentials on Khovanov-Rozansky homology. Geom. Topol., 19(6):3031–3104, 2015. doi:10.2140/gt.2015.19.3031. - [Sto09] Marko Stošić. Khovanov homology of torus links. Topology Appl., 156(3):533–541, 2009. doi:10.1016/j.topol.2008.08.004. - [Roz14] Lev Rozansky. An infinite torus braid yields a categorified Jones-Wenzl projector. Fund. Math., 225(1):305–326, 2014. doi:10.4064/fm225-1-14. - [Wen87] Hans Wenzl. On sequences of projections. C. R. Math. Rep. Acad. Sci. Canada, 9(1):5–9, 1987. - [Hog18] Matthew Hogancamp. Categorified Young symmetrizers and stable homology of torus links. Geom. Topol., 22(5):2943–3002, 2018. doi:10.2140/gt.2018.22.2943. - [GL15] Eugene Gorsky and Lukas Lewark. On stable sl3-homology of torus knots. Exp. Math., 24(2):162–174, 2015. doi:10.1080/10586458.2014.963746. - [OS05b] Peter Ozsváth and Zoltán Szabó. On knot Floer homology and lens space surgeries. Topology, 44(6):1281–1300, 2005. doi:10.1016/j.top.2005.05.001.",
  "source": "UnsolvedMath KP-1.31（kirby_low_dimensional_topology · topology）",
  "url": "https://unsolvedmath.com"
