  "detail": "Pick $x_1, \\dots, x_k \\in A_n$ at random. Is it true that, almost surely as $n \\to \\infty$, the random walk on this set of generators and their inverses equidistributes in time $O(n \\log n)$? This asks about mixing time for random walks on the alternating group with random generators. Determining optimal mixing times connects probability, group theory, and spectral graph theory.",
