  "detail": "Does there exist an odd perfect number? A perfect number is a positive integer that is equal to the sum of its proper divisors (excluding itself). For example, $6 = 1 + 2 + 3$ is perfect. While many even perfect numbers are known (the first few are 6, 28, 496, 8128), no odd perfect number has ever been found, despite extensive computer searches. It has been proven that if one exists, it must be greater than $10^{1500}$ and have at least 101 prime factors.",
