  "detail": "Are there infinitely many prime numbers of the form $M_p = 2^p - 1$ where $p$ is prime? Mersenne primes are primes of the form $2^p - 1$. As of 2024, only 51 Mersenne primes are known, with the largest being $2^{82,589,933} - 1$. It is conjectured that infinitely many exist, but this remains unproven. They are important for computational number theory and the GIMPS distributed computing project.",
