  "detail": "Besides 1, 8, and 144, are there any other perfect powers (numbers of the form $a^b$ where $a, b > 1$) in the Fibonacci sequence? The Fibonacci sequence has only three known perfect powers: $F_1 = F_2 = 1 = 1^n$, $F_6 = 8 = 2^3$, and $F_{12} = 144 = 12^2$. It is conjectured that these are the only ones, but this remains unproven despite extensive computational searches.",
