  "detail": "If $\\alpha$ is algebraic and irrational, and $\\beta$ is algebraic and irrational, is $\\alpha^\\beta$ transcendental? Hilbert's 7th problem (1900) was largely solved by Gelfond and Schneider independently in 1934 (Gelfond-Schneider theorem). However, cases involving non-algebraic irrational exponents remain open. For example, whether $e^e$ or $\\pi^\\pi$ are transcendental is unknown.",
