  "detail": "Every graph with chromatic number $k$ has a $K_k$ minor (where $K_k$ is the complete graph on $k$ vertices). The Hadwiger conjecture, proposed in 1943, generalizes the four color theorem. It has been proved for $k \\leq 6$ but remains open for $k \\geq 7$. The case $k=5$ is equivalent to the four color theorem.",
