  "detail": "What is the minimum number of colors needed to color the points of the plane such that no two points at distance 1 have the same color? It is known that this chromatic number is between 5 and 7. In 2018, Aubrey de Grey proved it is at least 5, but whether it is 5, 6, or 7 remains unknown.",
