  "summary": "What is the exact value of $R(5,5)$, the smallest number $n$ such that any 2-coloring of the edges of $K_n$ contains a monochromatic $K_5$?",
  "detail": "What is the exact value of $R(5,5)$, the smallest number $n$ such that any 2-coloring of the edges of $K_n$ contains a monochromatic $K_5$? Ramsey theory asks how large a structure must be to guarantee a certain property. The Ramsey number $R(5,5)$ is known to lie between 43 and 48, but the exact value remains unknown. As Joel Spencer said, \"Erdős asks us to imagine an alien force, demanding the value of $R(5,5)$ or they will destroy our planet... our best strategy is to get our best computers and mathematicians working on it.\"",
