  "detail": "Let $G$ be an abelian group of size $N$, and suppose that $A \\subset G$ has density $\\alpha$. Are there at least $\\alpha^{15}N^{10}$ tuples $(x_1, \\ldots, x_5, y_1, \\ldots, y_5) \\in G^{10}$ such that $x_i + y_j \\in A$ whenever $j \\in \\{i, i+1, i+2\\}$? This problem asks about higher-order additive structures in dense sets. Deng-Tidor-Zhao (2023) considered this problem and conjectured a negative answer, suggesting the exponent might not be optimal.",
