  "detail": "We call a group presentation finite if it represents a finite group. We say that a presentation is just finite if it is finite and is no longer finite on removal of any relation from it. Is it true that every finite group has a just finite presentation? Source: Kourovka Notebook, New Problems, 21st issue, 2026. Original problem number: 21.10. Discussion and literature: Note that if a group has a balanced presentation, then it is just finite. A similar argument can be applied for some p-groups using the Golod--Shafarevich inequality. Y. Barnea",
