  "summary": "If $\\kappa$ is a singular strong limit cardinal, then $2^\\kappa = \\kappa^+$.",
  "detail": "If $\\kappa$ is a singular strong limit cardinal, then $2^\\kappa = \\kappa^+$. The singular cardinals hypothesis, formulated by Paul Erdős and András Hajnal, concerns the behavior of the power set operation on infinite cardinals. It sits between the generalized continuum hypothesis and ZFC. Its consistency and independence status remains a major open problem in set theory.",
