  "proposer": "",
  "summary": "Does there exist a Jónsson algebra on $\\aleph_\\omega$?",
  "detail": "Does there exist a Jónsson algebra on $\\aleph_\\omega$? A Jónsson algebra is an algebraic structure with no proper subalgebra of the same cardinality. The existence of Jónsson algebras on various cardinals connects algebra with set theory. For $\\aleph_\\omega$ (the $\\omega$-th infinite cardinal), existence remains unknown. A positive answer would provide new insights into the algebraic structure of infinite sets and the behavior of singular cardinals.",
  "source": "UnsolvedMath ST-009（unknown set · set_theory）",
