  "detail": "Is the open coloring axiom (OCA) consistent with $2^{\\aleph_0} > \\aleph_2$? The open coloring axiom is a combinatorial principle with powerful consequences for the structure of the real line. It is known to be consistent with $2^{\\aleph_0} = \\aleph_2$, but consistency with larger values of the continuum is unknown. This problem explores the interaction between partition properties and cardinal arithmetic, central themes in modern set theory.",
