  "proposer": "",
  "summary": "How many Sudoku puzzles have exactly one solution?",
  "detail": "How many Sudoku puzzles have exactly one solution? Standard 9×9 Sudoku grids can be filled in approximately 6.67 × 10²¹ ways. A puzzle is a partial filling with a unique completion. Despite extensive computer searches, the exact count of puzzles with unique solutions remains unknown. This combinatorial problem involves constraints, symmetry breaking, and counting techniques. Understanding this would illuminate the mathematical structure underlying Sudoku and related constraint satisfaction problems.",
