  "summary": "What is the outcome of a perfectly played game of chess?",
  "detail": "What is the outcome of a perfectly played game of chess? Chess is a finite deterministic game, so theoretically one of three outcomes holds with perfect play: White wins, Black wins, or draw. Despite centuries of play and powerful computers, we don't know which. The game tree has approximately 10⁴⁷ positions, far beyond exhaustive analysis. Current evidence suggests a draw, but proving it requires breakthrough techniques in game-tree search, endgame databases, or mathematical analysis of chess positions.",
  "source": "UnsolvedMath GAME-005（unknown set · combinatorics）",
