  "summary": "Are the nim-sequences of all finite octal games eventually periodic?",
  "detail": "Are the nim-sequences of all finite octal games eventually periodic? Octal games are impartial combinatorial games defined by simple rules encoded in octal notation. Their nim-values (Grundy numbers) determine optimal play. For some octal games, the nim-sequence is eventually periodic; for others, patterns are elusive. Whether all finite octal games have eventually periodic nim-sequences is unknown. This problem connects game theory, number theory, and automata theory.",
