  "detail": "What is the optimal strategy for two agents to meet on a network without communication? The rendezvous problem asks: how should two agents move on a graph to minimize expected meeting time, when they can't communicate and may not know the graph structure? Variants include symmetric/asymmetric information, labeled/unlabeled nodes, and different graph families. Optimal strategies are known for some simple cases but remain open for general graphs. This problem bridges game theory, probability, and distributed algorithms.",
