  "detail": "For the Cartesian product of graphs $G \\square H$, is the domination number at least $\\gamma(G) \\cdot \\gamma(H)$? Vizing conjectured that the domination number of the Cartesian product of two graphs is at least the product of their domination numbers. This would give a lower bound on how efficiently one can dominate product graphs. The conjecture has been verified for many special cases but remains open in general. It has connections to network design and distributed computing.",
