  "detail": "Are there graphs on n vertices requiring more than floor(n/2) copies of each letter for word-representation? Word-representable graphs can be encoded by words where two vertices are adjacent if their letters alternate in the word. The question asks whether any graph needs more than half the number of vertices as copies of each letter. This connects graph theory to formal languages and combinatorics on words.",
