  "detail": "For r-partite r-uniform hypergraphs, is the vertex cover number at most (r-1) times the matching number? Ryser's conjecture relates the minimum transversal (vertex cover) size to maximum matching size in hypergraphs. For graphs (r=2) this is König's theorem. The conjecture proposes a tight bound for hypergraphs: τ ≤ (r-1)ν. This is a central open problem in hypergraph theory with connections to combinatorial optimization.",
